<ontology/use_chocolate_confectionery/use_chocolate_confectionery__doc_musk__q1/#resource> dcterms:bibliographicCitation "P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Products of the Vegetable Kingdom (1854; Project Gutenberg #15191), section CACAO OR COCOA" ;
    dcterms:source <https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/15191> ;
    a <ontology/EvidenceQuote/#resource> ;
    rdfs:label "Evidence for Musk used in Chocolate & Confectionery: P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Products of the Vegetable Kingdom (1854; Project Gutenberg #15191), section CACAO OR COCOA"@en ;
    <ontology/quoteText/#resource> "The Mexicans, in preparing the chocolate paste, add some long pepper, a little annatto, and lastly vanilla; some add cinnamon, cloves and anise, and those who love perfumes, musk and ambergris."@en ;
    <ontology/retrievalMode/#resource> "direct_sentence" .
